    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk we dont use scps in this account. i checked the bucket policy too and there's nothing in there that says deny. it just feels like something is lurking in the background blocking it. it's like the request is just getting snatched away right when it tries to hit the bucket. is there like a way to trace exactly which layer is rejecting the call? like a log or something that shows why the access was denied?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right to suspect something is lurking, and the best way to find out is to trace the actual request. You can enable AWS CloudTrail logging for S3, which will record every API call made to your bucket, including the identity that made it and the exact error code returned. This trail will tell you precisely *why* the request was rejected, which is much more specific than a general \"Access Denied.\" Look for the `errorCode` in the CloudTrail event details; it will point you toward the specific policy failure.",
      "source": "target",
